[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186134138 :question/answer-fields 17592186130984] {:db/id 17592186133929 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" "question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" "question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/id #uuid "3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/math-academy-id "q-162577" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=3,$ $y=-1,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=4.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=y{e}^{x}\\,i+{z}^{2}\\,j+3z\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3z) \\\\  & =y{e}^{x}+0+3 \\\\  & =y{e}^{x}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(y{e}^{x}+3)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,y{e}^{x}+3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" "answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" "answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" "answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" "answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" :answer/id #uuid "0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" :answer/id #uuid "4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y{e}^{x}+2z+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer/id #uuid "83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y{e}^{x}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" :answer/id #uuid "555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7" :answer/id #uuid "4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/id #uuid "e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/math-academy-id "q-162587" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the finite solid region enclosed by the planes $y=-1,$ $y=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=2,$ and the surfaces $x=y-z$ and $x=1+{y}^{2}.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=i+x{z}^{3}\\,j+xz\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz) \\\\  & =0+0+x \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type II solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,y-z\\le x\\le 1+{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/id #uuid "498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" "answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" "answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" "answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" "answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" :answer/id #uuid "36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\,3x{z}^{2}+z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" :answer/id #uuid "2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" :answer/id #uuid "0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,3x{z}^{2}+z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer/id #uuid "54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad" :answer/id #uuid "847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/id #uuid "a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-162579" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=2,$ $y=1,$ $y=3,$ $z=1,$ $z=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=x\\sqrt{y}\\,i-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+xy\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}+0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/id #uuid "19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" "answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" "answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" "answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" "answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" :answer/id #uuid "282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" :answer/id #uuid "dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer/id #uuid "4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" :answer/id #uuid "493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b" :answer/id #uuid "3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134136 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}+0+0 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type II solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,y-2z\\le x\\le 4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y-2z}^{4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}\\,{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281503 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z) \\\\  & =1+(-2)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type I solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le z\\le {x}^{2}+y\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{{x}^{2}+y}\\,{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/id #uuid "3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834"] ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/math-academy-id "q-162577"] ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=3,$ $y=-1,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=4.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=y{e}^{x}\\,i+{z}^{2}\\,j+3z\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?"] ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3z) \\\\  & =y{e}^{x}+0+3 \\\\  & =y{e}^{x}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(y{e}^{x}+3)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,y{e}^{x}+3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074"] ["answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" :answer/id #uuid "0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1"] ["answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1" :answer/value "y+3"] ["answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" :answer/id #uuid "4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a"] ["answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a" :answer/value "y{e}^{x}+2z+3"] ["answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer/id #uuid "83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005"] ["answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005" :answer/value "y{e}^{x}+3"] ["answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" :answer/id #uuid "555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2"] ["answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2" :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2z"] ["answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7" :answer/id #uuid "4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7"] ["answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7" :answer/value "{e}^{x}+y"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/correct "answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/choices "answer-0bc77a23-0eee-55f5-af88-ab3ad6a354e1"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/choices "answer-4bb5a8f6-ed9a-5ef1-aebf-3359a8c0719a"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/choices "answer-83db7844-9dcf-556d-9a9a-daf1ca164005"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/choices "answer-555ab874-d0dc-5e4c-a1b1-97fc4821c9e2"] ["answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074" :answer-field/choices "answer-4c276ef4-b454-5573-8609-3f6090682ed7"] ["question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2ef39217-f0e4-532f-b400-3709c241a074"] [17592186133929 :knowledge-point/questions "question-3d423292-2025-559a-9094-6ebc6fb41834"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/id #uuid "e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/math-academy-id "q-162587"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the finite solid region enclosed by the planes $y=-1,$ $y=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=2,$ and the surfaces $x=y-z$ and $x=1+{y}^{2}.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=i+x{z}^{3}\\,j+xz\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS=\n$$"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz) \\\\  & =0+0+x \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type II solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,y-z\\le x\\le 1+{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/id #uuid "498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50"] ["answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" :answer/id #uuid "36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d"] ["answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\,3x{z}^{2}+z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" :answer/id #uuid "2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc"] ["answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" :answer/id #uuid "0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165"] ["answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,3x{z}^{2}+z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer/id #uuid "54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800"] ["answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad" :answer/id #uuid "847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad"] ["answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-z}^{1+{y}^{2}}\\,{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/correct "answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/choices "answer-36efeb09-1895-56f2-887a-74b67306458d"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/choices "answer-2a1a0b26-5443-5a61-939e-04dd145cbdfc"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/choices "answer-0eed31b1-1432-5919-b43b-eb4ed1548165"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/choices "answer-54b2d94d-d3b1-5e20-863e-0f3029049800"] ["answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50" :answer-field/choices "answer-847aa225-9761-56bc-b061-f790278ac3ad"] ["question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-498c1fb4-5fbe-531d-bc45-e785a72a6f50"] [17592186133929 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e44dc84b-de4c-5508-b285-9f3d93ffdc55"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/id #uuid "a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-162579"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=2,$ $y=1,$ $y=3,$ $z=1,$ $z=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=x\\sqrt{y}\\,i-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+xy\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}+0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/id #uuid "19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61"] ["answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" :answer/id #uuid "282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f"] ["answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f" :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}+y"] ["answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" :answer/id #uuid "dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090"] ["answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090" :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}+x"] ["answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer/id #uuid "4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a"] ["answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a" :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}"] ["answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" :answer/id #uuid "493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc"] ["answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc" :answer/value "\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{1}{y}+x"] ["answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b" :answer/id #uuid "3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b"] ["answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b" :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/correct "answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/choices "answer-282ca48e-2a60-5aa5-a7ef-5e8ccb1a7c1f"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/choices "answer-dde34e84-5b46-56e1-87f0-de42f2772090"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/choices "answer-4e92e89f-6a0f-5b5c-9cc9-2174221f6a2a"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/choices "answer-493526e7-2497-5843-9007-3650fcadb2fc"] ["answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61" :answer-field/choices "answer-3a51c99c-bb63-5030-af27-f60c30a2ad6b"] ["question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-19af3f29-aebd-50f6-b224-a1f92ead3b61"] [17592186133929 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a809785e-b48f-5cb0-92f3-ff24733e01ab"] [17592186134136 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}+0+0 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type II solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,y-2z\\le x\\le 4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y-2z}^{4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}\\,{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186281503 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z) \\\\  & =1+(-2)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type I solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le z\\le {x}^{2}+y\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{{x}^{2}+y}\\,{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "retractions" [[17592186134136 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}+0+0 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type II solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,y-2z\\le x\\le 4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y-2z}^{4-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}\\,{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186281503 :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z) \\\\  & =1+(-2)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type I solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le z\\le {x}^{2}+y}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{{x}^{2}+y}\\,{x}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186134138 :question/answer-fields 17592186130984]]}]